<section class="section" id="story">
  <div class="wrap story-grid">
    <div class="story-copy reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Our Story</span>
      <h2>Sejak hari ini.<br /><span class="translation">Since day one.</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Juandi — most people know him as Andi — started NIR-MA-TA as a single
        cart on the roadside in Senggigi. No electricity, no fancy machine.
        Beans ground by hand, espresso pulled by hand, brewed to order for
        whoever pulled up a stool.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        Travellers kept stopping. They kept coming back. Some left a sticker on
        the cart on their way out — you'll still find them plastered across it,
        from every corner of the world. Over a year on the road, that one cart
        earned a perfect run of 5-star reviews. Now it's a shop of its own,
        right next to the money exchange on Jl. Raya Senggigi — same coffee,
        same conversation, same guy.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="story-quote">
        <p>
          "Awesome coffee made from fresh local beans. Best espresso I've had
          in Lombok. Made without electricity — <strong>just gas and muscle</strong>
          on a manual espresso machine, with proper extraction technique."
        </p>
        <cite>— Dominik Krchnavy, Google review</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <div class="story-stats reveal-stagger">
      <div class="stat card">
